    "shot": {
      "description": "shot --project_id ID --at 3:50 | --words "…" [--live]: one instant on all three time bases (103e/1:43 edited, 125.3r raw, 10.4s source) — project id, revision, dirty flag, visible layers with sizes and anchors, transcript ±5 s, nearest cuts, staged proposals in range, and one image: the saved render by default, or --live seeks the editor and grabs the live canvas frame. The reply says which (image.source + evidence). A --live image carries image.frame_settled and image.freshness: "settled" when the frame is proven to postdate the seek; "possibly_stale" with image.freshness_note otherwise (frame_settled is false on older shells — never silent).",
      "input_schema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
