    },
    "verify": {
      "description": "verify --range a b: decode the real media at every cut and overlay edge in the edited-time range with ffmpeg. cut.clipped-word (error) when the level 0–120 ms after an out point stays within 15 dB of the word tail; frame.black/frame.identical (warning) from sampled frames. Frames plus a filmstrip with waveforms land in --out or the agent cache. Times accept m:ss.s and e/r/s suffixes. Read-only; at most 100 edges per run. Exits 0 with findings present: read data.findings/data.counts, not the exit code. A data.status of 'unavailable' means the range was NOT content-verified (see the error-level content.unavailable findings) — never a pass.",
      "input_schema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
